*   **Schedule 1 (Additional Income and Adjustments to Income):** This is where your business income (from Schedule C) and your allowable Student Loan Interest deduction are reported.
*   **Schedule 2 (Additional Taxes):** This is where your self-employment tax (from Schedule SE) is attached to your return.

*(Note: Because your interest and dividends total $1,370, which is under the $1,500 threshold, you are not strictly required to file Schedule B, though you still must report the $890 and $480 on the front page of your Form 1040).*
